Summary of modifications relative to the upstream coding setting
-----------------------------------------------------------------
* sample/llm_policy_rollout.py  - rewritten as a multi-step "execute -> feedback
  -> fix" agent rollout with persistent vLLM engines, per-trajectory
  termination (success / no-improvement / max-steps) and step-level records.
* reward/llm_rl_reward.py, reward/advantage.py - dual-dimension step reward
  (GT pass ratio + weighted synthetic-test pass ratio) and step-level
  group-relative advantages; extended training/eval metrics.
* train/coding_train.py - adapted from the upstream trainer (PPO-clip + K3 KL
  objective is upstream); added per-batch padding trim, prompt-length
  filtering that keeps rewards aligned, KL / clip-fraction / loss logging and
  crash-safe checkpoint swapping.
* common/sandbox.py - rewrite of the upstream process-based executor as a
  shared batched scheduler: chunked concurrency, queue draining for large
  outputs, two-level (judge / hard-kill) timeouts, best-effort hardening.
* common/safe_io.py, sample/build_tasks.py - new: atomic + file-locked JSON
  persistence and persistent per-node task state.
* coding_rl.py, coding_eval.py, sample/llm_env_rollout.py, reward/execute.py,
  reward/rl_aggregate_data.py, train/utils.py - adapted to the above
  (resume from progress.json, env-task acceptance, independent re-judging).

train/lr_schedulers.py and train/log_utils.py contain code from the
HuggingFace / Optuna authors (Apache-2.0); their original headers are kept.
